<task id="205a" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration — row A38a (H4 KV manifest secret-free omit (A38a — filter-served-entries via FileKvSecretManifest + extend ficOmitSecretNames seam))</title>
    <phase>Phase Pre-Live-Fire — Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration (task 205, A38a re-scope 2026-08-25)</phase>
    <gate>ready</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Row A38a scope is auth-tagged (H4/H4-shared KV secrets credential-type seam on FR-39) and modifies `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/**` PLUS adds unit + integration tests under `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/**` — TEST-MODIFYING override per project CLAUDE.md §8.5 triggers unconditional FULL rigor (code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5) irrespective of default classification. Credential-selection blast-radius: a wrong served-entry filter produces the "secret beneath MI-FIC absorbing a broken FIC with green health" failure mode (remediation plan §8) undetectable at runtime. Peer escalation 2026-08-25 already fired the `partial-omit-set-discovered` trigger on the prior A38 attempt — A38a is the manifest-half re-scope that MUST land bundled with A38b.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>fable</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Explicit user directive per remediation plan §8 Fable/Opus tier posture: "A38 + A42 on Fable/Opus (credential-selection seam + cross-worktree reconciliation — auth-tagged, FULL rigor, code-review + adr-check unconditional); rest Sonnet-5 @ high". A38a inherits the tier because (a) credential-logic blast radius (every future customer's authentication path — this is not a Sonnet-5 literal-execution shape), (b) served-entry filter over the LIVE FileKvSecretManifest must respect the BINDING invariant at FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151 without weakening it (subtle abstraction placement), (c) Model 1 vs Model 2 fleet-consistency semantics (N per-customer vaults, marker-consistency detection) require design judgment beyond mechanical translation, (d) commit-bundle coordination with A38b (customer.bicep gate) demands architectural awareness of the H2a→H4 sequencing.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Code-only under src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/** + tests; disjoint from 205b A42 (EntraAppReg/**), 205g A38b (infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep), 205h A38c (scripts/*.ps1), 205i A44.5 (EnvVarValues/**). All 5 may run concurrently.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>A35 (landed via 28c2c1b38); **205g A38b (customer.bicep gate) MUST land in the same commit bundle** — A38a manifest omit alone re-opens the false-migrated trap because H2a re-seeds via customer.bicep on every Model 2 deploy</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, auth, code, control-plane, credential-seam, fr-39, file-kv-secret-manifest, filter-served-entries</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4h (per peer escalation re-scope 2026-08-25, owner approved)</estimated-effort>
