  <prompt>Apply row A38a — the MANIFEST HALF of the peer-escalated A38 re-scope (2026-08-25, owner approved 2026-08-25). On secret-free environments (`RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`), FILTER SERVED ENTRIES from the LIVE `FileKvSecretManifest` (Worker/Program.cs:449 — `StaticKvSecretManifest` is interim/revert-only and MUST NOT be edited) for three targets: `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`. The manifest.yaml row for `BFF-API-ClientSecret` MUST REMAIN unchanged — `FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` BINDING invariant refuses to serve ANY entries unless `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `Dataverse-ClientSecret` are both present with `never_delete=true`. Omit is a served-entry filter DOWNSTREAM of that invariant check, NOT a yaml row deletion. EXTEND the existing FR-39 `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` / `OmitCanonicalNames` seam at `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179 + :366` (landed via task 126) — add the three omit targets to the omit-set that already flows through `KvSecretWriteRequest.OmitCanonicalNames` → `KvSecretWriteAction.Omitted`. DO NOT invent a parallel seam. Both H4 (per-tenant, for `BFF-API-ClientSecret` `from-existing-kv`) and H4-shared (for `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` + `AiSearch--AdminKey` `from-shared-service` per manifest.yaml:255/:433) MUST honor the omit uniformly. Positive migration marker MUST be applied idempotently as BOTH a KV resource tag (`spaarke-secret-free-identity=true`) AND a `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field (`sprk_credentialmode=secret-free`) — under Model 2 fan-out, marker applies ONCE PER VAULT in the existing per-customer iteration loop. Fleet-consistency detector (T8-probe-shape or manifest-linter class) MUST detect the missed-tag case on N per-customer vaults. `Dataverse-ClientSecret` STAYS unconditionally (Q3 Path A rollback copy until 2026-11-23 sunset). A23 clobber guard (skip-if-absent + never-declared) already peer-grep-confirmed intact — MUST NOT regress. `appsettings.template.json` `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` KV-ref is auth-v4 obligation 051-E (deferred to 2026-11-23); A44 owns the consumer guard — NOT touched here. This POML MUST land bundled with 205g A38b — the executor commits changes to the working tree but MUST NOT run any git commit; the main session commits the bundle atomically. Amend punch-list annotations for A38a.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE L2 control-plane handler author + KV secrets manifest expert + credential-selection seam specialist. Expert in: `FileKvSecretManifest` (LIVE per Worker/Program.cs:449) reading `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` (26 entries; canonical single-source-of-truth per task 084); the `IKvSecretManifest` contract + `KvSecretEntry(name, operation, valueSource, ServiceRef)` record + `KvSecretOperation.Upsert` + `KvSecretValueSource` (`FromBicepOutput` / `FromExistingKvSecret` / `FromRunParameters` / `Generated` / `FromSharedService`); `FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` BINDING invariant (never delete manifest.yaml row for `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `Dataverse-ClientSecret`); the FR-39 `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` / `OmitCanonicalNames` seam (task 126, `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179 + :366`); H4 handler (per-tenant, dispatches `from-existing-kv` entries incl. `BFF-API-ClientSecret`) vs H4-shared handler (dispatches `from-shared-service` entries incl. `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`); `KvSecretsPopulationOptions` envelope; Model 1 (single shared vault) vs Model 2 (per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` × N vaults) dispatch; ADR-028 A4 secret-free BFF-identity contract + §9.1 sentinel ruling (OMIT-is-the-signal, never sentinel — sentinel → opaque `AADSTS7000215`); FR-39 pluggable credential seam + FR-40 invariant I6; A23 clobber guard (`skip-if-absent` + `never-declared`) — grep-confirmed intact by peer; §6.5 record 2026-08-25 (Path C for `BFF-API-ClientSecret` prong 1 = never-create/seed/restore in secret-free envs; `Dataverse-ClientSecret` Path A rollback copy until 2026-11-23).</role>

  <goal>The three A38a omit targets (`BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`) are EXCLUDED from the served entries returned by `FileKvSecretManifest.ReadAsync(...)` when `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` — but the manifest.yaml rows themselves remain unchanged (FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151 BINDING invariant preserved intact). The three omit targets ARE INCLUDED when an explicit Q3 Path A rollback flag is set (regression path). Extension MUST be to the existing `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179` `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` seam + `:366` `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet (task 126 landed) — the new omit targets are added to that pre-existing set, NOT via a parallel new seam. H4-shared handler honors the same omit uniformly for `from-shared-service` entries (SB-conn + admin-key per manifest.yaml:255/:433) — do NOT skip the from-shared-service half. Positive migration marker mechanism landed: BOTH a KV resource tag (`spaarke-secret-free-identity=true`) applied by H4/H4-shared handler AND a `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field (`sprk_credentialmode=secret-free`) written by handler — marker application is idempotent (re-run yields same state). Under Model 2 fan-out, marker is applied ONCE PER VAULT in the existing per-customer iteration loop — N vaults, all consistent. Fleet-consistency detector (T8-probe-shape or manifest-linter class per remediation plan §5.3) detects the missed-tag case on N per-customer vaults. Unit + integration tests assert: served-entry filter, marker idempotency, Model 2 N-vault marker consistency, missed-tag detection, A23 clobber guard preserved, `Dataverse-ClientSecret` unaffected under both branches. `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` UNCHANGED (peer explicitly identified this as revert-only interim; the LIVE reader is FileKvSecretManifest). `FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` BINDING invariant PRESERVED (never delete yaml row). `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` + `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` succeed. Executor commits changes to working tree but DOES NOT run `git commit` — main session commits A38a + A38b bundle atomically.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Peer escalation record 2026-08-25 (notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md "A38 execution record" block lines 76-107): the prior A38 attempt (task 205a) fired the `partial-omit-set-discovered` trigger at grep-verify Step 2 because the peer discovered 5 live upsert sites beyond `StaticKvSecretManifest`: (1) `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep:705 + :713` — `kvSecretValues` map UNCONDITIONALLY seeds `AiSearch--AdminKey` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` on EVERY Model 2 H2a deploy (BEFORE H4 runs), (2) `scripts/Rotate-Secrets.ps1:590 + :663` — rotation resurrects `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` with no secret-free gate, (3) `scripts/Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1:123 + :178` — operator seeding writes both, (4) `scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1:533` — legacy 13-step orchestrator writes SB-conn, (5) `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74` — interim/revert-only. Peer + owner declared the site inventory COMPLETE 2026-08-25 and approved a full 4-way split: A38a (manifest — THIS POML), A38b (customer.bicep gate — 205g), A38c (scripts — 205h), A44.5 (H7/task-142 half of A30 sentinel contract — 205i). Peer also discovered critical design facts: LIVE reader is `FileKvSecretManifest` (Worker/Program.cs:449), NOT `StaticKvSecretManifest` (which is interim/revert-only per task 126 comment block); manifest.yaml `BFF-API-ClientSecret` is `from-existing-kv` (line 118) → per-tenant H4 handler; manifest.yaml `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` (line 255) + `AiSearch--AdminKey` (line 433) are `from-shared-service` → H4-shared handler; `FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` carries a BINDING invariant that REFUSES to serve ANY entries unless `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `Dataverse-ClientSecret` are both present in yaml with `never_delete=true` — hence the omit design MUST filter SERVED ENTRIES downstream of that invariant check, not delete yaml rows; and `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179` already defines `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey = "ficOmitSecretNames"` + `:366` already threads `omitCanonicalNames` → `KvSecretWriteRequest.OmitCanonicalNames` → `KvSecretWriteAction.Omitted` (landed via task 126) — A38a MUST extend THAT seam, not invent a parallel one. §6.5 record (APPROVED owner 2026-08-25): `Dataverse-ClientSecret` STAYS unconditionally as Q3 Path A rollback copy until 2026-11-23 sunset — Q3 Path A rollback flag re-includes ONLY the three A38a targets, never `Dataverse-ClientSecret` (which is already unconditional and independently governed). Critical BINDING SEQUENCING: A38a manifest omit ALONE re-opens the false-migrated trap because H2a re-seeds via customer.bicep on every Model 2 deploy — A38a MUST commit-bundle with A38b (customer.bicep gate) atomically or the run reports "omitted/migrated" in H4 records while the same run's H2a step has already seeded both secrets (the exact peer-cited failure). Model 1 (single shared vault) is trivially fleet-consistent; Model 2 fans out to N per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` vaults where a missed tag on one vault is itself a silent-skip failure (remediation plan §5.3 fleet-consistency gap). `appsettings.template.json` `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` KV-ref is auth-v4 obligation 051-E deferred to 2026-11-23 — punch row A44 owns the consumer guard, NOT A38a.</background>
