  <constraints>
    <constraint source="peer escalation record 2026-08-25 — LIVE reader">MUST target `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` (LIVE per `Worker/Program.cs:449`) — NOT `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` (interim/revert-only per task 126 comment block). Any edit to `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` is a rule violation; STOP + escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151 BINDING invariant">MUST filter SERVED ENTRIES from `ReadAsync(...)`; MUST NOT delete manifest.yaml rows. The :151 invariant refuses to serve ANY entries unless `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `Dataverse-ClientSecret` yaml rows are present with `never_delete=true`. Filter must occur DOWNSTREAM of that invariant check (e.g. inside the entry-emission loop or in a post-load filter step in the same class), NOT by removing entries from the yaml. If a naive extension appears to require yaml row deletion, STOP + reconcile — the invariant must not be weakened.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 126 FR-39 seam already-landed">MUST extend the existing `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179` `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey = "ficOmitSecretNames"` + `:366` `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet seam (task 126 landed). The three A38a omit targets are ADDED to that pre-existing set, NOT via a parallel new seam. If A38a is tempted to define a new `RequireSecretFreeIdentity` bool parameter as the primary mechanism, that is fine — but the actual omit MUST flow through the existing `OmitCanonicalNames` seam so the writer receives them uniformly via `KvSecretWriteRequest.OmitCanonicalNames` → `KvSecretWriteAction.Omitted`. Parity with task 125's FR-39 "no special-casing" commitment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="peer escalation record 2026-08-25 — StaticKvSecretManifest revert-only">MUST NOT touch `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs`. Peer explicitly identified this as revert-only interim (kept in-tree solely to enable emergency rollback of the FileKvSecretManifest DI-swap). Any edit here would defeat that purpose.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §9.1 sentinel ruling">MUST NOT sentinel any of the three secret entries on secret-free envs. Sentinel value produces opaque `AADSTS7000215` at runtime — indistinguishable from a real misconfiguration. OMIT is the signal. Migration marker MUST live outside the credential slot: KV resource tag AND `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 obligation 051-E (deferred to 2026-11-23)">MUST NOT touch `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.template.json` `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` KV-ref. That is auth-v4 obligation 051-E deferred to 2026-11-23; punch row A44 owns the consumer guard. A38a is manifest-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="marker mechanism — §9.1 + design intent">Positive migration marker MUST be applied as BOTH (a) a KV resource tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity=true` for infra-scan detectability AND (b) a `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field `sprk_credentialmode=secret-free` for provisioning-run auditability. Marker application is idempotent (re-run yields same state — check-then-apply pattern, not blind write). Under Model 2 fan-out, marker is applied ONCE PER VAULT in the existing per-customer iteration loop inside H4-shared (do not add a new iteration — hook into the existing dispatch).</constraint>
    <constraint source="A23 clobber guard peer grep-confirmed intact">MUST NOT regress `skip-if-absent` (`Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1:1088`, `kv-secrets.generated.bicep:35`) + `never-declared` (`Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1:1079`, `kv-secrets.generated.bicep:26`) semantics. After A38a edit, re-run peer's grep and confirm both terms still present + still exercised by existing tests. The existing A23 test-name churn should be ZERO.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§6.5 record 2026-08-25 (APPROVED owner) — Dataverse-ClientSecret STAYS">MUST NOT alter `Dataverse-ClientSecret` manifest entry, served-entry emission, or add it to the omit-set. It STAYS unconditionally as Q3 Path A time-boxed rollback copy until 2026-11-23 sunset. Only the three A38a targets change. Also MUST NOT reclassify `FromBicepOutput` / `FromExistingKvSecret` / `FromRunParameters` / `Generated` / `FromSharedService` value-source classification for any entry — the change is a served-entry filter, not a classification change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="H4-shared uniform honoring">The `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` MUST honor the omit uniformly for `from-shared-service` entries (`ServiceBus-ConnectionString` per manifest.yaml:255, `AiSearch--AdminKey` per manifest.yaml:433). Do NOT skip the from-shared-service half — if omitted only from H4, SB-conn + admin-key remain re-seeded by H4-shared. If H4-shared lacks an equivalent omit-honoring path, ADD one (mirror `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:366`'s `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet plumbing).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">Edits to `.claude/**` (e.g. `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md` §6.5 EDIT package prong 1 rewrite if not yet landed) MUST occur in the MAIN SESSION. A38a code edits are safe for sub-agent execution; document any `.claude/**` follow-up as a coord item — do NOT attempt Edit/Write on `.claude/**` paths from a sub-agent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 component justification">Any NEW file created (e.g. a `ManifestLinter.cs`, `SecretFreeEnvMarker.cs`, or new test file) MUST cite row A38a in the file header + answer Existing / Extension / Cost-of-doing-nothing. Prefer EXTENDING `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` + `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs` + `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs` over new sibling files.</constraint>
    <constraint source="commit-bundle sequencing — BINDING">MUST NOT run `git commit` — the executor commits changes to the working tree but the MAIN SESSION commits the bundle atomically with 205g A38b. A38a alone re-opens the false-migrated trap because H2a re-seeds via customer.bicep on every Model 2 deploy (peer-cited failure). If Wave-3F-072 or similar automation tries to commit A38a solo, STOP + escalate for main-session bundle coordination.</constraint>
    <constraint source="verification obligation (post-A35 re-verify)">If the manifest generator or H4 handlers have been refactored since 2026-08-25 (last peer verification), re-verify `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179` `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` + `:366` `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet threading + `FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` BINDING invariant location BEFORE editing. Do NOT assume prior grep results still hold.</constraint>
  </constraints>

