    <step order="3" name="Design the served-entry filter + option surface">Author (scratchpad first, then code) the design: (a) EXTEND `KvSecretsPopulationOptions` with a new `bool RequireSecretFreeIdentity` (default false) — mirrors the BFF App Service setting `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`. (b) The three A38a target names live in a `static readonly IReadOnlySet&lt;string&gt;` constant on `FileKvSecretManifest` (or a nearby internal class) named e.g. `SecretFreeIdentityOmitTargets` — enumerates `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`. (c) FileKvSecretManifest.ReadAsync flow: after yaml load + :151 BINDING invariant check + entry emission loop, if `_options.Value.RequireSecretFreeIdentity` is true, FILTER emitted entries excluding names in `SecretFreeIdentityOmitTargets`. Entry set returned to caller is thus smaller by exactly 3 on secret-free envs. yaml rows unchanged; :151 invariant unchanged. (d) H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler pipes the omit set through the EXISTING `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` / `OmitCanonicalNames` seam at :179/:366 — either by adding the three names to the operator's ficOmitSecretNames run-parameter automatically when RequireSecretFreeIdentity is set, or by unioning them into the omitCanonicalNames HashSet before it feeds KvSecretWriteRequest. This preserves task 125/126's "no special-casing" commitment — writer still receives the same OmitCanonicalNames shape. (e) H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler mirrors the union (mandatory — SB-conn + admin-key travel through H4-shared per from-shared-service). If H4-shared lacks an OmitCanonicalNames-equivalent, ADD it. Document design in code comments citing row A38a + §9.1 + peer escalation record.</step>
