    <step order="6" name="Extend H4 + H4-shared handlers — union into existing OmitCanonicalNames seam + apply marker">Edit `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs`: (a) read `_options.Value.RequireSecretFreeIdentity`; if true, union `SecretFreeIdentityOmitTargets` into the existing `omitCanonicalNames` HashSet at :366. This keeps the KvSecretWriteRequest.OmitCanonicalNames path identical (task 125's "no special-casing" preserved). (b) Apply positive migration marker: KV resource tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity=true` via ArmClient (idempotent check-then-apply — read existing tag, no-op if already set) + `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field write `sprk_credentialmode=secret-free` via IProvisioningRunRepository or equivalent (idempotent). Edit `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs`: (a) if a mirror `OmitCanonicalNames` seam exists, union the same set; if not, ADD one (mirror H4's :179 constant + :366 threading). (b) In the per-customer iteration loop (Model 2 fan-out), apply the KV tag marker ONCE PER VAULT — hook into the existing iteration; do NOT add a new pass. (c) Log marker application at Information level with vault ID for fleet-consistency auditing.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Checkpoint (after 3 code-edit steps)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="8" name="Add fleet-consistency detector — Model 2 missed-tag case">Author a lightweight detector (either a `ManifestLinter` class OR extend `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` post-fan-out step): after iterating N per-customer vaults, cross-check that every vault has the `spaarke-secret-free-identity=true` KV tag (or all lack it uniformly — mixed state is the failure). If mixed, log Warning with vault-ID list + emit a failure record (do NOT throw — this is a detector, not a fatal gate; expose via run report). If a full detector class is warranted for testability, extract as `SecretFreeMarkerConsistencyDetector.cs` with §11 justification citing row A38a + remediation plan §5.3 fleet-consistency gap.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Add / extend tests">Extend or create the following test files: (a) `FileKvSecretManifestTests.cs` — assert manifest EXCLUDES the three targets when `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`; INCLUDES them when false; :151 BINDING invariant still fires when yaml rows missing (regression protection); `Dataverse-ClientSecret` stays in both branches. (b) `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandlerTests.cs` — assert `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet contains the three targets after secret-free unioning; existing FR-39 ficOmitSecretNames operator-parameter path still works; marker (KV tag + state field) applied idempotently (2nd invocation is a no-op). (c) `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandlerTests.cs` — assert Model 2 fan-out applies marker to N=3 vaults uniformly; missed-tag detection fires when one vault lacks the tag (via detector from Step 8); from-shared-service entries (SB-conn + admin-key) actually omitted under secret-free. (d) A23 clobber guard tests still green (unchanged — regression protection). (e) Regression test: `Dataverse-ClientSecret` STAYS in both branches (Q3 Path A protected).</step>
    <step order="9.5" name="Quality gates — code-review + adr-check (unconditional per TEST-MODIFYING override + auth tag)">Run `code-review` skill on the diff (focus: FileKvSecretManifest served-entry filter placement vs :151 invariant; H4-shared uniform honoring; marker idempotency; A23 no-regress). Run `adr-check` skill — MUST verify ADR-028 A4 compliance (A4 landed via A35). Fix Critical + High findings; if any finding requires an ADR exception, invoke root CLAUDE.md §6.5 protocol.</step>
