  <escalation>
    <trigger name="site-inventory-drifted" source="peer escalation record 2026-08-25 (site inventory declared complete)">If ANY NEW upsert site for `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, or `AiSearch--AdminKey` is discovered beyond the 5 peer-inventoried sites (customer.bicep:705/713 → A38b, Rotate-Secrets.ps1:588/661 → A38c, Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1:123/178 → A38c, Provision-Customer.ps1:533 → A38c, StaticKvSecretManifest interim), STOP + escalate — the site inventory was declared complete per peer 2026-08-25. New site changes the omit-set completeness proof and MUST be handled before A38a lands.</trigger>
    <trigger name="binding-invariant-blocks-filter" source="FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151 BINDING invariant">If FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151 BINDING invariant blocks the filter (e.g. appears to require yaml row for the omit-target to be present in served set), reconcile by adding a served-entry filter DOWNSTREAM of the invariant check (inside the entry-emission loop or as a post-load filter step), NOT by removing or weakening the invariant. If placement is genuinely impossible without weakening :151, STOP + escalate as an architectural conflict.</trigger>
    <trigger name="manifest-refactored-since-2026-08-25" source="verification obligation">If H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs seam has been refactored since 2026-08-25 (verify by re-grepping `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` + `OmitCanonicalNames`), reconcile with latest before extending. Do NOT assume prior grep results still hold. Same for FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151 invariant location.</trigger>
    <trigger name="h4-shared-omit-path-missing" source="from-shared-service uniform honoring obligation">If H4-shared handler does not have an equivalent OmitCanonicalNames-honoring path, ADD it (mirror H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179 constant + :366 threading). Do NOT skip the from-shared-service half — SB-conn + admin-key would remain re-seeded by H4-shared otherwise, defeating A38a entirely.</trigger>
    <trigger name="peer-execution-record-amended" source="canonical spec source drift check">If the peer's execution record (notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md "A38 execution record" block, lines 76-107) has been amended since 2026-08-25 (owner or peer added new findings, additional sites, or scope changes), re-read for updated site inventory + scope before applying edits.</trigger>
    <trigger name="dataverse-clientsecret-in-omit-set" source="§6.5 record 2026-08-25 + Q3 sunset 2026-11-23">If executor is tempted to omit `Dataverse-ClientSecret` alongside the three A38a targets (e.g. because it is a "client secret" and appears to fit the pattern), STOP. `Dataverse-ClientSecret` is Q3 Path A rollback copy until 2026-11-23; it STAYS unconditionally. Only the three A38a targets are omitted.</trigger>
    <trigger name="marker-in-credential-slot" source="§9.1 sentinel ruling">If executor is tempted to write a marker string ("MI-FIC", "SECRET_FREE", "REDACTED", etc.) INTO the KV secret slot instead of applying it as a KV tag or state field, STOP. §9.1 rules this out — sentinel resolution produces opaque `AADSTS7000215` at runtime. Marker MUST live outside the credential slot.</trigger>
    <trigger name="static-manifest-edit-attempted" source="peer escalation record 2026-08-25 — revert-only interim">If any edit is attempted on `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs`, STOP + revert. It is peer-identified revert-only interim kept in-tree solely to enable emergency rollback of the FileKvSecretManifest DI-swap. Any A38a-related change there defeats that purpose.</trigger>
    <trigger name="a23-clobber-guard-regressed" source="row A23 already-applied + peer grep-confirmed intact 2026-08-25">If the edit accidentally removes `skip-if-absent` or `never-declared` semantics (or their tests), STOP + revert. A23 protects against exactly the class of clobber a naive omit could re-open. Peer confirmed intact 2026-08-25 — regression here is high-severity.</trigger>
    <trigger name="git-commit-attempted" source="commit-bundle sequencing BINDING constraint">If the executor is tempted to run `git commit` (either directly or via a helper script or Wave-3F-072 automation), STOP. A38a MUST NOT commit solo — it re-opens the false-migrated trap because H2a re-seeds via customer.bicep on every Model 2 deploy (peer-cited failure). Only the main session commits the A38a + A38b bundle atomically.</trigger>
    <trigger name="claude-directory-write-required" source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">If executor is a sub-agent and any `.claude/**` file needs to be updated to match the A38a contract, STOP + note as coord item for main session — do NOT attempt Edit/Write on `.claude/**` paths from a sub-agent.</trigger>
    <trigger name="fleet-consistency-detector-cannot-land-in-budget" source="remediation plan §5.3 fleet-consistency gap">If the Model 2 missed-tag detector (Step 8) cannot land within the 4h budget, file a follow-up row in `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` + note in run report. Do NOT silently defer — silence is the anti-pattern §9.1 exists to prevent.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep for `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey` in `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` returns them in a `SecretFreeIdentityOmitTargets` (or equivalently-named) set used to FILTER served entries; the manifest.yaml rows are UNCHANGED (grep manifest.yaml — all three rows still present with unchanged classifications).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` BINDING invariant PRESERVED: grep confirms the check block still refuses to serve entries unless `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `Dataverse-ClientSecret` yaml rows are present with `never_delete=true`. Its location/behavior is unchanged by A38a.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` UNCHANGED by A38a: `git diff HEAD -- src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` returns empty diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179` + `:366` seam EXTENDED (not parallel-invented): grep confirms `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` + `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet still present at their line-anchor locations (or their post-refactor equivalents); the three A38a targets are unioned into that HashSet when `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`. Zero occurrences of a NEW parameter key besides possibly `RequireSecretFreeIdentity` (the option surface, not a parallel omit seam).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` honors the omit uniformly for `from-shared-service` entries: unit test asserts SB-conn + admin-key are excluded from H4-shared write actions when `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Dataverse-ClientSecret` STAYS unconditionally in served entries under BOTH `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` and false — assertions present + green in tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No sentinel value ("SECRET_FREE", "MI-FIC", "REDACTED", "OMITTED", or similar) is written into any of the three KV secret slots — grep confirms zero occurrences of such tokens as `KvSecretEntry(...)` values for the three target names.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Positive migration marker mechanism landed: BOTH (a) KV resource tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity=true` applied by H4/H4-shared handler AND (b) `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field `sprk_credentialmode=secret-free` written by handler. Both are idempotent (verified by test that 2nd invocation is a no-op).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Model 2 fan-out: unit test with N=3 vaults asserts marker (KV tag) is applied uniformly to all N vaults, hooked into the existing per-customer iteration in H4-shared (not a new pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fleet-consistency detector (T8-probe-shape or manifest-linter class) fires when one vault lacks the tag: unit test with mixed vault state (2 tagged, 1 not) asserts detector logs Warning + emits failure record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A23 clobber guard preserved: post-edit grep confirms `skip-if-absent` + `never-declared` (or their code equivalents) still present in `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` + `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` at previously peer-confirmed line anchors; existing A23 tests still pass unchanged (zero A23 test-name churn).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` succeeds with zero errors. `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` succeeds with all new + existing tests green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Punch list row A38a in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` has `last_known_status_after_execution` annotated with source sites edited + marker mechanism + Model 1/2 verified + A23 preserved + FR-39 seam extended (not parallel-invented) + :151 BINDING invariant preserved + commit-bundle READY status.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Executor DID NOT run `git commit` — verifiable via commit log (no new commit authored by executor) + explicit statement in Step 13 report; main-session bundle-commit coordination requested.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`appsettings.template.json` `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` KV-ref UNTOUCHED by A38a: `git diff HEAD -- src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.template.json` returns empty diff for the SB-conn line (auth-v4 obligation 051-E owns it; A44 owns the consumer guard).</criterion>
