  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11 three-question template). **Existing**: `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` is the LIVE `IKvSecretManifest` per Worker/Program.cs:449 (task 126 DI-swap over interim StaticKvSecretManifest); `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs:179 + :366` already carries the FR-39 `FicOmitSecretNamesParameterKey` / `OmitCanonicalNames` seam (landed via task 126); `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` is the from-shared-service dispatch point with existing per-customer iteration for Model 2 fan-out; `KvSecretsPopulationOptions` is the existing options envelope; A23 clobber guard (`skip-if-absent` + `never-declared`) is peer-grep-confirmed intact in the manifest generator area; `FileKvSecretManifest.cs:151` BINDING invariant governs manifest.yaml row presence for `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `Dataverse-ClientSecret`. A38a EXTENDS all these — no new sibling components except (optionally) a `SecretFreeMarkerConsistencyDetector` for Model 2 fleet-consistency (with §11 justification in its file header if separated). **Extension**: Adding a `RequireSecretFreeIdentity` bool to `KvSecretsPopulationOptions` + a `SecretFreeIdentityOmitTargets` constant + a served-entry filter step in FileKvSecretManifest.ReadAsync DOWNSTREAM of the :151 invariant + unioning the three targets into H4's existing `OmitCanonicalNames` HashSet + adding the equivalent path to H4-shared + hooking a marker-application step (KV tag + state field) into H4/H4-shared handlers' existing dispatch. Task 125/126's "no special-casing" commitment preserved — the writer still receives the same `KvSecretWriteRequest.OmitCanonicalNames` shape via the same seam. **Cost-of-doing-nothing**: A38a is the MANIFEST HALF of the full A38 re-scope closure (peer escalation 2026-08-25, owner approved 2026-08-25). BLOCKS-186 as part of the A38-family (A38a + A38b + A38c + A44.5). Without A38a, H4/H4-shared serves the three secret-slot entries on every run, and the writer upserts them regardless — every H4 run silently reverses the auth-v4 migration (§10.1 Δ1/Δ2) while reporting green in the run record. Concrete failure modes without A38a: (1) fresh Model 2 customer boots on FIC per Δ3 A39 settings but H4 STILL upserts admin-key + client-secret + SB conn-string → "secret beneath MI-FIC absorbing a broken FIC with green health" (remediation plan §8 — auth-v4-identified "strictly worse than no migration"); (2) A38a extension of task 126's FR-39 seam is the pluggable-mechanism completion — without it, task 126's seam sits unused for its stated purpose. Extension of task 126's FR-39 seam is the mandatory shape per task 125's "no special-casing" commitment — inventing a parallel seam would fragment authority over the omit contract. Cost-of-doing-nothing-manifest-only: manifest-only omit is WORSE than no change if H2a re-seeds (peer's proof: customer.bicep:705/:713 UNCONDITIONALLY writes both `AiSearch--AdminKey` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` on every Model 2 H2a deploy — BEFORE H4 runs). Hence A38a is INCOMPLETE alone: it MUST land bundled with 205g A38b (customer.bicep gate) in one atomic commit — the "H2a re-seeded, H4 omitted, run reports migrated" false-positive is the exact failure the escalation caught. Rule: prong 3 of §6.5 record narrows to `spaarkedev1` + any as-yet-unprovisioned Model 2 stamp; per Q6, no Model 2 stamp will be provisioned before A36-A42 land — so A38a + A38b's omit contract holds for 100% of new provisioning traffic.</notes>

